menu "espix usb"

    config ESPIX_USB_VERBOSE
        bool "Verbose USB host logging"
        depends on ESPIX_USB_ROLE_HOST
        default n
        help
            Raise the USB stack's own log tags to DEBUG, so `dmesg` shows what
            the host library and the class drivers think is happening: port
            changes, what was enumerated and at what speed, and why a device was
            not claimed by any driver.

            This is the switch to reach for when a device does not appear. The
            stack logs everything useful at DEBUG and almost nothing at INFO, so
            with this off a working enumeration and an empty socket look
            identical -- which is exactly the question it exists to answer.

            Two halves, and both are needed. CONFIG_LOG_MAXIMUM_LEVEL (DEBUG, in
            sdkconfig.defaults) decides whether the messages exist in the image
            at all; this option raises the tags that are noisy enough to be worth
            leaving off by default.

            Costs nothing when off, and when on it costs log volume: the kernel
            log ring holds 96 lines (ESPIX_KLOG_LINES) and this will fill it.
            Nothing else in the system is raised -- WiFi, lwip and the app loader
            keep their own levels.

endmenu